Usage: dd [OPTION]...

Convert and copy a file with specified block size and count.

OPTIONS:
  if ARG         read from FILE instead of stdin
  of ARG         write to FILE instead of stdout
  ibs ARG        read up to BYTES bytes at a time
  obs ARG        write BYTES bytes at a time
  bs ARG         read and write up to BYTES bytes at a time
  cbs ARG        convert BYTES bytes at a time
  count ARG      copy only N input blocks
  skip ARG       skip N ibs-sized input blocks
  seek ARG       skip N obs-sized output blocks
  iseek ARG      same as skip=N
  oseek ARG      same as seek=N
  conv ARG       convert as per comma-separated symbol list
  status ARG     control diagnostic output
  iflag ARG      read as per comma-separated symbol list
  oflag ARG      write as per comma-separated symbol list
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
